{"content":"# Fixed — an explicit `compactionSettings` pin now beats the bench env

The PR-description contract was the intended one, so the code was changed
to match it (`lib/src/cli/agent_cli.dart`,
`_effectiveCompactionSettings`):

```dart
final override = config.compactionSettings;
if (override != null) return override;
return resolveBenchCompactionSettings(
  resolveCompactionHostWiring(
    mainModel: _agent.state.model,
    contextWindowCap: config.contextWindowCap,
  ).settings,
  window: _effectiveContextWindow,
  env: environment,
);
```

`FAH_COMPACT_TRIGGER_TOKENS` retunes the DEFAULTS for a bench run; it
never rewrites a user-pinned section — including `enabled: false` (the
knob cannot re-enable compaction the user switched off). The in-code
comment now states this explicitly, and the behavior is again
byte-identical to pre-gh-1604 whenever a section is pinned.

Pinned by a new group in `test/cli/agent_cli_bench_compaction_test.dart`
through a `@visibleForTesting` seam (`effectiveCompactionSettingsForTest`):

- explicit pin + env → the pin verbatim (reserve/keep untouched);
- explicit `enabled: false` pin + env → stays disabled;
- no pin + env → the trigger applies (regression anchor);
- no pin + no env → `CompactionSettings.forWindow` defaults.
